    {
      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "First, let's determine the length of one side of the square. Since a square has four equal sides, and the perimeter is the sum of all four sides, we can set up the equation:\n\n\\[ \\text{Perimeter} = 4 \\times \\text{side length} \\]\n\nWe know the perimeter is 32 feet, so:\n\n\\[ 32 = 4 \\times \\text{side length} \\]\n\nTo find the side length, we divide both sides by 4:\n\n\\[ \\text{side length} = \\frac{32}{4} = 8 \\text{ feet} \\]\n\nNow that we know each side of the square is 8 feet long, we can calculate the area of the square. The area \\( A \\) of a square is given by the formula:\n\n\\[ A = \\text{side length}^2 \\]\n\nSubstituting the side length we found:\n\n\\[ A = 8^2 = 64 \\text{ square feet} \\]\n\nThus, the area of the square is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{64}\n\\]",
